    "rationale": "Tempo and meter are AGREED after the re-tap \u2014 121.06 BPM, meter 7, ratio x1.01 against both backends, which closes the octave error BUG-102 was filed about. What remains is phase: the taps sit a systematic -42.3 ms (librosa) / -44.7 ms (madmom) early, and the two backends agree with each other to within 2.4 ms. It is not the rig \u2014 bleed was tapped in the same session on the same calibration and lands at -13.6 / -0.4 ms, and every other track is inside +/-32 ms. On a track whose pulse is carried by a syncopated bass riff, Matt consistently feels the beat ~45 ms ahead of where onset detectors place it. Phosphene is a visualizer: a preset should fire where a listener feels the pulse, not where an onset detector fires. So the taps are the truth and the backends' phase is declined."
